recovery from the system Trash if needed\n\n# NEVER dismiss warnings/errors as \"pre-existing\" or \"not from our changes\".\n# ALWAYS fix ALL warnings and errors you encounter, regardless of whether you introduced them.\n# No excuses - just fix them.\n\n# BEFORE running release, deploy, build, or any repetitive workflow:\n# - ALWAYS check for existing .sh scripts first (release.sh, deploy.sh, build.sh, etc.)\n# - Use `ls *.sh` or `glob **/*.sh` in the project root\n# - If a script exists for the task, USE IT instead of doing steps manually\n# - Scripts contain the correct sequence of steps (version bumps, changelog, tagging, etc.)\n# - Doing it manually risks missing steps (like updating version.dart)\n\n# NEVER invent fictional URLs, repos, links, or external references.\n# ALWAYS verify that URLs and external resources actually exist BEFORE using them.\n# If you don't have a verified URL, ask the user or mark it as placeholder/coming soon.\n# currentDate\nToday's date is 2026-02-23.\n\n      IMPORTANT: this context may or may not be relevant to your tasks. You should not respond to this context unless it is highly relevant to your task.\n</system-reminder>\n"
