ogin \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"email\":\"test@example.com\",\"password\":\"securepass123\"}'\n```\nExpected: 200, JSON with user data, `Set-Cookie` header. Save the token.\n\n**Test 3: Get current user (authenticated)**\n```bash\ncurl -X GET http://localhost:8080/api/auth/me \\\n  -H \"Cookie: session_token=<TOKEN_FROM_LOGIN>\"\n```\nExpected: 200, JSON with user details.\n\n**Test 4: Create a todo (authenticated)**\n```bash\ncurl -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/todos \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -H \"Cookie: session_token=<TOKEN>\" \\\n  -d '{\"title\":\"Buy groceries\"}'\n```\nExpected: 201, JSON with the created todo including `user_id`.\n\n**Test 5: List todos (authenticated)**\n```bash\ncurl -X GET http://localhost:8080/api/todos \\\n  -H \"Cookie: session_token=<TOKEN>\"\n```\nExpected: 200, JSON with array of todos belonging to this user only.\n\n**Test 6: Update a todo**\n```bash\ncurl -X PUT http://localhost:8080/api/todos/1 \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -H \"Cookie: session_token=<TOKEN>\" \\\n  -d '{\"completed\":true}'\n```\nExpected: 200, JSON with updated todo.\n\n**Test 7: Get single todo**\n```bash\ncurl -X GET http://localhost:8080/api/todos/1 \\\n  -H \"Cookie: session_token=<TOKEN>\"\n```\nExpected: 200, JSON with todo details.\n\n**Test 8: Delete a todo**\n```bash\ncurl -X DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/todos/1 \\\n  -H \"Cookie: session_token=<TOKEN>\"\n```\nExpected: 200, confirmation message.\n\n**Test 9: Access without auth (should fail)**\n```bash\ncurl -X GET http://localhost:8080/api/todos\n```\nExpected: 401, `{\"error\": \"Authentication required\"}`.\n\n**Test 10: Cross-user isolation**\nRegister a second user, create todos with that user, then try to access them with the first user's session. Expected: 404 for all operations on the other user's todos.\n\n**Test 11: Logout**\n```bash\ncurl -v -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/logout \\\n  -H \"Cookie: session_token=<TOKEN>\"\n```\nExpected: 200, `Set-Cookie` with `Max-Age=0` to expire the cookie. Subsequent requests with the same token should return 401.\n\n**Test 12: Duplicate registration (should fail)**\n```bash\ncurl -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/register \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\"email\":\"test@example.com\",\"password\":\"anotherpass\",\"name\":\"Dupe User\"}'\n```\nExpected: 409, `{\"error\": \"Email already registered\"}`.\n\n---\n\n### Implementation Sequence\n\nThe recommended order of implementation is:\n\n1. **Project creation** (`duxt create todo --mode=server`)\n2. **Add dependencies** to `pubspec.yaml`, run `dart pub get`\n3. **Models** (User, Todo, Session) -- so the ORM can auto-migrate tables\n4. **Utils** (password.dart, session_manager.dart) -- foundational helpers\n5. **Middleware** (auth_middleware.dart) -- depends on session_manager\n6. **Auth API** (auth.dart) -- depends on models, utils, middleware\n7. **Todo API** (todos.dart) -- depends on models, middleware\n8. **Server entry point** (server/main.dart) -- wires everything together\n9. **Test** with `duxt dev` and curl commands\n\n---\n\n### Potential Challenges and Mitigations\n\n1. **Response.json `status` and `headers` parameters**: The exact parameter names for setting HTTP status codes and headers on `Response.json()` need to be verified against the actual Duxt API. If the signature differs, it may be `Response.json(body, statusCode: 201)` or require constructing a `Response` manually with headers.\n\n2. **req.context for passing user data**: If `req.context` is not a mutable map in Duxt's request object, an alternative approach would be to return the `User` from the middleware function directly and have route handlers accept it as a parameter.\n\n3. **Cookie header access**: If `req.headers` returns headers differently (e.g., lowercase only, or via a method), the cookie extraction code may need adjustment.\n\n4. **ORM create/update return types**