              "prompt": "Design an implementation plan for building a REST API with session-based authentication in a Duxt (Dart) project at /Users/flakerimi/TMP/todo (currently empty directory).\n\n## What we know from Duxt docs:\n\n### Project Structure (server mode):\n```\nmy-app/\n├── pubspec.yaml\n├── duxt.yaml                 # mode: server\n├── lib/\n│   ├── main.dart\n│   ├── app.dart\n│   ├── pages/\n│   ├── layouts/\n│   ├── components/\n│   └── models/               # ORM models\n├── server/\n│   ├── main.dart             # DuxtServer setup\n│   └── api/                  # API route handlers\n├── database/\n│   └── database.sqlite\n```\n\n### Model pattern (extends Model with tableName, schema, fromMap, toMap):\n```dart\nimport 'package:duxt_orm/duxt_orm.dart';\n\nclass User extends Model {\n  @override\n  String get tableName => 'users';\n\n  @override\n  Map<String, ColumnType> get schema => {\n      'email': ColumnType.text,\n      'password': ColumnType.text,\n      'name': ColumnType.text,\n  };\n\n  String? email;\n  String? password;\n  String? name;\n\n  @override\n  void fromMap(Map<String, dynamic> map) {\n    super.fromMap(map);\n    email = map['email'] as String?;\n    password = map['password'] as String?;\n    name = map['name'] as String?;\n  }\n\n  @override\n  Map<String, dynamic> toMap() {\n    return {\n      ...super.toMap(),\n      'email': email,\n      'password': password,\n      'name': name,\n    };\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### API route pattern:\n```dart\nimport 'package:duxt/duxt.dart';\n\nvoid registerApi(DuxtServer server) {\n  server.get('/api/todo', (req) async {\n    return Response.json({'message': 'Todo list'});\n  });\n\n  server.post('/api/todo', (req) async {\n    final body = await req.body();\n    return Response.json({'message': 'Todo created', 'data': body});\n  });\n\n  server.get('/api/todo/:id', (req) async {\n    final id = req.params['id'];\n    return Response.json({'message': 'Todo detail', 'id': id});\n  });\n\n  server.put('/api/todo/:id', (req) async {\n    final id = req.params['id'];\n    final body = await req.body();\n    return Response.json({'message': 'Todo updated', 'id': id, 'data': body});\n  });\n\n  server.delete('/api/todo/:id', (req) async {\n    final id = req.params['id'];\n    return Response.json({'message': 'Todo deleted', 'id': id});\n  });\n}\n```\n\n### CLI:\n- `duxt create todo --mode=server` to create project\n- `duxt g model <Name> <field:type>...` to generate models\n- `duxt scaffold <Name> <field:type>...` to generate full CRUD\n- `duxt dev` to start dev server\n\n### Key features:\n- Duxt ORM auto-migrates tables (creates tables, adds missing columns)\n- SQLite for dev, PostgreSQL/MySQL for production\n- Middleware can protect routes (auth checks, redirects)\n- Built-in security: CSRF protection, rate limiting, etc.\n- File-based routing for pages, explicit registration for API routes\n\n## Requirements:\n1. **User model**: email (unique), password (hashed), name\n2. **Todo model**: title, completed (bool), user_id (int, FK to users)\n3. **Auth API**: POST /api/auth/register, POST /api/auth/login, POST /api/auth/logout, GET /api/auth/me\n4. **Todo CRUD API**: All protected by session auth - GET /api/todos, POST /api/todos, GET /api/todos/:id, PUT /api/todos/:id, DELETE /api/todos/:id\n5. **Session-based auth**: Server-side sessions with cookies\n6. **Password hashing**: bcrypt or similar\n7. **Middleware**: Auth middleware to protect Todo routes\n8. **Users can only access their own todos**\n\nPlease design a detailed step-by-step implementation plan covering:\n- Project scaffolding (CLI commands)\n- All files to create/modify with their paths\n- Model definitions\n- API route implementations\n- Auth middleware\n- Session management approach\n- Password hashing approach\n- Dependencies needed in pubspec.yaml\n- How to test the API end-to-end\n"
