                "type": "text",
                "text": "\n\nI now have enough information gathered from the Duxt documentation to produce a comprehensive implementation plan. Let me present the full plan.\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Plan: REST API with Session-Based Authentication in Duxt\n\n### Overview\n\nThis plan covers building a Todo REST API with session-based authentication in a Duxt server-mode project at `/Users/flakerimi/TMP/todo`. The application will have User and Todo models, session-based auth with cookies, auth middleware to protect Todo routes, and per-user data isolation.\n\n---\n\n### Phase 1: Project Scaffolding\n\n**Step 1.1: Create the Duxt server project**\n\n```bash\ncd /Users/flakerimi/TMP\nduxt create todo --mode=server\n```\n\nThis generates the standard server project structure including `server/`, `lib/models/`, `server/api/`, `pubspec.yaml`, and `duxt.yaml`.\n\n**Step 1.2: Generate the User model via CLI**\n\n```bash\ncd /Users/flakerimi/TMP/todo\nduxt g model User email:string password:string name:string\n```\n\nCreates `lib/models/user.dart`.\n\n**Step 1.3: Generate the Todo model via CLI**\n\n```bash\nduxt g model Todo title:string completed:bool user_id:int\n```\n\nCreates `lib/models/todo.dart`.\n\n**Step 1.4: Generate the Session model via CLI**\n\n```bash\nduxt g model Session token:string user_id:int expires_at:string\n```\n\nCreates `lib/models/session.dart`. This model stores server-side sessions in the database.\n\n**Step 1.5: Add dependencies to `pubspec.yaml`**\n\nAfter project creation, add the following dependencies for password hashing and UUID generation:\n\nFile: `/Users/flakerimi/TMP/todo/pubspec.yaml`\n\nAdd under `dependencies`:\n```yaml\ndependencies:\n  # ... existing duxt dependencies from create command ...\n  dbcrypt: ^1.0.0     # bcrypt password hashing for Dart\n  uuid: ^4.0.0        # UUID generation for session tokens\n```\n\nThen run `dart pub get`.\n\n> **Note on package choices**: `dbcrypt` is a pure Dart bcrypt implementation that works without native bindings. `uuid` is the standard Dart package for generating unique session tokens. Both are available on pub.dev.\n\n---\n\n### Phase 2: Model Definitions\n\n**Step 2.1: Customize the User model**\n\nFile: `/Users/flakerimi/TMP/todo/lib/models/user.dart`\n\nThe CLI-generated model will be close to what is needed. Customize it to ensure the structure is correct:\n\n```dart\nimport 'package:duxt_orm/duxt_orm.dart';\n\nclass User extends Model {\n  @override\n  String get tableName => 'users';\n\n  @override\n  Map<String, ColumnType> get schema => {\n    'email': ColumnType.text,\n    'password': ColumnType.text,\n    'name': ColumnType.text,\n  };\n\n  String? email;\n  String? password;\n  String? name;\n\n  @override\n  void fromMap(Map<String, dynamic> map) {\n    super.fromMap(map);\n    email = map['email'] as String?;\n    password = map['password'] as String?;\n    name = map['name'] as String?;\n  }\n\n  @override\n  Map<String, dynamic> toMap() {\n    return {\n      ...super.toMap(),\n      'email': email,\n      'password': password,\n      'name': name,\n    };\n  }\n\n  /// Return a safe representation without the password hash\n  Map<String, dynamic> toSafeMap() {\n    return {\n      'id': id,\n      'email': email,\n      'name': name,\n      'created_at': createdAt?.toIso8601String(),\n      'updated_at': updatedAt?.toIso8601String(),\n    };\n  }\n}\n```\n\nKey design decisions:\n- `toSafeMap()` is a custom helper that excludes the password hash from API responses. This prevents accidentally leaking sensitive data.\n- The `super.fromMap(map)` / `super.toMap()` calls handle the base fields `id`, `created_at`, `updated_at` that the ORM provides automatically.\n\n**Step 2.2: Customize the Todo model**\n\nFile: `/Users/flakerimi/TMP/todo/lib/models/todo.dart`\n\n```dart\nimport 'package:duxt_orm/duxt_orm.dart';\n\nclass Todo extends Model {\n  @override\n  String get tableName => 'todos';\n\n  @override\n  Map<String, ColumnType> get schema => {\n    'title': ColumnType.text,\n    'completed': ColumnType.boolean,\n    'user_id': ColumnType.integer,\n  };\n\n  String? title;\n  bool? completed;\n  int? userId;\n\n  @override\n  void fromMap(Map<String, dynamic> map) {\n    super.fromMap(map);\n    title = map['title'] as String?;\n    completed = map['completed'] as bool?;\n    userId = map['user_id'] as int?;\n  }\n\n  @override\n  Map<String, dynamic> toMap() {\n    return {\n      ...super.toMap(),\n      'title': title,\n      'completed': completed,\n      'user_id': userId,\n    };\n  }\n}\n```\n\nKey notes:\n- `user_id` is the foreign key column in the database, mapped to `userId` in Dart (convention).\n- `completed` defaults to `false` when creating new todos (handled in the API layer).\n\n**Step 2.3: Create the Session model**\n\nFile: `/Users/flakerimi/TMP/todo/lib/models/session.dart`\n\n```dart\nimport 'package:duxt_orm/duxt_orm.dart';\n\nclass Session extends Model {\n  @override\n  String get tableName => 'sessions';\n\n  @override\n  Map<String, ColumnType> get schema => {\n    'token': ColumnType.text,\n    'user_id': ColumnType.integer,\n    'expires_at': ColumnType.text,\n  };\n\n  String? token;\n  int? userId;\n  String? expiresAt;\n\n  @override\n  void fromMap(Map<String, dynamic> map) {\n    super.fromMap(map);\n    token = map['token'] as String?;\n    userId = map['user_id'] as int?;\n    expiresAt = map['expires_at'] as String?;\n  }\n\n  @override\n  Map<String, dynamic> toMap() {\n    return {\n      ...super.toMap(),\n      'token': token,\n      'user_id': userId,\n      'expires_at': expiresAt,\n    };\n  }\n\n  bool get isExpired {\n    if (expiresAt == null) return true;\n    return DateTime.parse(expiresAt!).isBefore(DateTime.now());\n  }\n}\n```\n\nDesign decisions for sessions:\n- **Database-backed sessions**: Stored in a `sessions` table rather than in-memory, so sessions survive server restarts and work across multiple server instances.\n- **`expires_at` as text**: Stored as ISO 8601 string for SQLite compatibility (SQLite has no native datetime type).\n- **`isExpired` helper**: Convenience getter for checking session validity in the auth middleware.\n- **Session token**: Will be a UUID v4, stored both in the database and sent to the client as a cookie.\n\n---\n\n### Phase 3: Password Hashing Utility\n\n**Step 3.1: Create a password helper**\n\nFile: `/Users/flakerimi/TMP/todo/server/utils/password.dart`\n\n```dart\nimport 'package:dbcrypt/dbcrypt.dart';\n\nclass PasswordHelper {\n  static final _bcrypt = DBCrypt();\n\n  /// Hash a plaintext password using bcrypt\n  static String hash(String password) {\n    final salt = _bcrypt.gensaltWithRounds(12);\n    return _bcrypt.hashpw(password, salt);\n  }\n\n  /// Verify a plaintext password against a bcrypt hash\n  static bool verify(String password, String hash) {\n    return _bcrypt.checkpw(password, hash);\n  }\n}\n```\n\nWhy bcrypt:\n- Industry standard for password hashing with built-in salt and configurable work factor.\n- `dbcrypt` is a pure Dart implementation -- no native dependencies needed.\n- 12 rounds provides good security/performance balance.\n\n---\n\n### Phase 4: Session Management\n\n**Step 4.1: Create a session manager**\n\nFile: `/Users/flakerimi/TMP/todo/server/utils/session_manager.dart`\n\n```dart\nimport 'package:duxt_orm/duxt_orm.dart';\nimport 'package:uuid/uuid.dart';\nimport '../../lib/models/session.dart';\nimport '../../lib/models/user.dart';\n\nclass SessionManager {\n  static const _sessionDuration = Duration(hours: 24);\n  static final _uuid = Uuid();\n\n  /// Create a new session for a user. Returns the session token.\n  static Future<String> createSession(int userId) async {\n    final token = _uuid.v4();\n    final expiresAt = DateTime.now().add(_sessionDuration).toIso8601String();\n\n    final sessions = Model<Session>(Session());\n    final session = Session()\n      ..token = token\n      ..userId = userId\n      ..expiresAt = expiresAt;\n    await sessions.create(session.toMap());\n\n    return token;\n  }\n\n  /// Look up a session by token. Returns the User if valid, null if expired/missing.\n  static Future<User?> getUserFromToken(String token) async {\n    final sessions = Model<Session>(Session());\n    final results = await sessions.where({'token': token}).get();\n    if (results.isEmpty) return null;\n\n    final session = results.first;\n    if (session.isExpired) {\n      // Clean up expired session\n      await sessions.delete(session.id!);\n      return null;\n    }\n\n    final users = Model<User>(User());\n    final user = await users.find(session.userId!);\n    return user;\n  }\n\n  /// Delete a session (logout)\n  static Future<void> deleteSession(String token) async {\n    final sessions = Model<Session>(Session());\n    final results = await sessions.where({'token': token}).get();\n    if (results.isNotEmpty) {\n      await sessions.delete(results.first.id!);\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nDesign decisions:\n- **24-hour session duration**: Reasonable default; configurable via constant.\n- **UUID v4 tokens**: Cryptographically random, effectively unguessable.\n- **Lazy cleanup**: Expired sessions are deleted when encountered. A production system would add a periodic cleanup job.\n- **Duxt ORM Query API**: Uses `Model<T>` with `.where()` and `.find()` following the ActiveRecord pattern from the Duxt ORM docs.\n\n---\n\n### Phase 5: Auth Middleware\n\n**Step 5.1: Create the auth middleware**\n\nFile: `/Users/flakerimi/TMP/todo/server/middleware/auth_middleware.dart`\n\n```dart\nimport 'package:duxt/duxt.dart';\nimport '../utils/session_manager.dart';\nimport '../../lib/models/user.dart';\n\n/// Extracts the session token from the cookie header, validates it,\n/// and attaches the authenticated User to the request context.\n/// Returns a 401 Response if no valid session is found.\nFuture<dynamic> authMiddleware(Request req) async {\n  final cookieHeader = req.headers['cookie'] ?? '';\n  final token = _extractSessionToken(cookieHeader);\n\n  if (token == null) {\n    return Response.json(\n      {'error': 'Authentication required'},\n      status: 401,\n    );\n  }\n\n  final user = await SessionManager.getUserFromToken(token);\n  if (user == null) {\n    return Response.json(\n      {'error': 'Invalid or expired session'},\n      status: 401,\n    );\n  }\n\n  // Attach user to request context for downstream handlers\n  req.context['user'] = user;\n  return null; // null means \"continue to the route handler\"\n}\n\n/// Parse the Cookie header to extract the session_token value.\nString? _extractSessionToken(String cookieHeader) {\n  if (cookieHeader.isEmpty) return null;\n  final cookies = cookieHeader.split(';').map((c) => c.trim());\n  for (final cookie in cookies) {\n    if (cookie.startsWith('session_token=')) {\n      return cookie.substring('session_token='.length);\n    }\n  }\n  return null;\n}\n```\n\nMiddleware design:\n- **Return null to continue**: Following the Duxt middleware pattern, returning `null` lets the request pass through to the route handler. Returning a `Response` short-circuits and sends that response immediately.\n- **`req.context['user']`**: Attaches the authenticated `User` object so route handlers can access it without re-querying the database.\n- **Cookie parsing**: Manual extraction from the `Cookie` header since Duxt works with raw headers. The cookie name is `session_token`.\n\n---\n\n### Phase 6: Auth API Routes\n\n**Step 6.1: Create auth API routes**\n\nFile: `/Users/flakerimi/TMP/todo/server/api/auth.dart`\n\n```dart\nimport 'package:duxt/duxt.dart';\nimport 'package:duxt_orm/duxt_orm.dart';\nimport '../../lib/models/user.dart';\nimport '../utils/password.dart';\nimport '../utils/session_manager.dart';\nimport '../middleware/auth_middleware.dart';\n\nvoid registerAuthApi(DuxtServer server) {\n\n  // POST /api/auth/register\n  server.post('/api/auth/register', (req) async {\n    final body = await req.body();\n\n    final email = body['email'] as String?;\n    final password = body['password'] as String?;\n    final name = body['name'] as String?;\n\n    // Validation\n    if (email == null || email.isEmpty ||\n        password == null || password.isEmpty ||\n        name == null || name.isEmpty) {\n      return Response.json(\n        {'error': 'Email, password, and name are required'},\n        status: 400,\n      );\n    }\n\n    if (password.length < 8) {\n      return Response.json(\n        {'error': 'Password must be at least 8 characters'},\n        status: 400,\n      );\n    }\n\n    // Check for existing user\n    final users = Model<User>(User());\n    final existing = await users.where({'email': email}).get();\n    if (existing.isNotEmpty) {\n      return Response.json(\n        {'error': 'Email already registered'},\n        status: 409,\n      );\n    }\n\n    // Create user with hashed password\n    final hashedPassword = PasswordHelper.hash(password);\n    final userData = {\n      'email': email,\n      'password': hashedPassword,\n      'name': name,\n    };\n    final user = await users.create(userData);\n\n    // Create session\n    final token = await SessionManager.createSession(user.id!);\n\n    return Response.json(\n      {'message': 'Registration successful', 'user': user.toSafeMap()},\n      status: 201,\n      headers: {\n        'Set-Cookie': 'session_token=$token; HttpOnly; Path=/; '\n            'SameSite=Strict; Max-Age=86400',\n      },\n    );\n  });\n\n  // POST /api/auth/login\n  server.post('/api/auth/login', (req) async {\n    final body = await req.body();\n\n    final email = body['email'] as String?;\n    final password = body['password'] as String?;\n\n    if (email == null || password == null) {\n      return Response.json(\n        {'error': 'Email and password are required'},\n        status: 400,\n      );\n    }\n\n    // Find user by email\n    final users = Model<User>(User());\n    final results = await users.where({'email': email}).get();\n    if (results.isEmpty) {\n      return Response.json(\n        {'error': 'Invalid email or password'},\n        status: 401,\n      );\n    }\n\n    final user = results.first;\n\n    // Verify password\n    if (!PasswordHelper.verify(password, user.password!)) {\n      return Response.json(\n        {'error': 'Invalid email or password'},\n        status: 401,\n      );\n    }\n\n    // Create session\n    final token = await SessionManager.createSession(user.id!);\n\n    return Response.json(\n      {'message': 'Login successful', 'user': user.toSafeMap()},\n      headers: {\n        'Set-Cookie': 'session_token=$token; HttpOnly; Path=/; '\n            'SameSite=Strict; Max-Age=86400',\n      },\n    );\n  });\n\n  // POST /api/auth/logout\n  server.post('/api/auth/logout', (req) async {\n    final cookieHeader = req.headers['cookie'] ?? '';\n    final token = _extractToken(cookieHeader);\n\n    if (token != null) {\n      await SessionManager.deleteSession(token);\n    }\n\n    return Response.json(\n      {'message': 'Logged out successfully'},\n      headers: {\n        'Set-Cookie': 'session_token=; HttpOnly; Path=/; '\n            'SameSite=Strict; Max-Age=0',\n      },\n    );\n  });\n\n  // GET /api/auth/me (protected)\n  server.get('/api/auth/me', (req) async {\n    final result = await authMiddleware(req);\n    if (result != null) return result; // 401 response\n\n    final user = req.context['user'] as User;\n    return Response.json({'user': user.toSafeMap()});\n  });\n}\n\nString? _extractToken(String cookieHeader) {\n  if (cookieHeader.isEmpty) return null;\n  final cookies = cookieHeader.split(';').map((c) => c.trim());\n  for (final cookie in cookies) {\n    if (cookie.startsWith('session_token=')) {\n      return cookie.substring('session_token='.length);\n    }\n  }\n  return null;\n}\n```\n\nDesign decisions for auth endpoints:\n- **Registration**: Validates input, checks for duplicate email (409 Conflict), hashes password with bcrypt, creates user, auto-creates session and sets cookie so the user is logged in immediately after registration.\n- **Login**: Finds user by email, verifies password hash, creates new session. Generic error message \"Invalid email or password\" to prevent email enumeration.\n- **Logout**: Deletes the server-side session record and expires the cookie (`Max-Age=0`).\n- **GET /me**: Uses the auth middleware inline. This is for the single protected auth endpoint; the todo routes use middleware more systematically.\n- **Cookie security flags**: `HttpOnly` (no JS access), `SameSite=Strict` (CSRF protection), `Path=/` (sent for all routes), `Max-Age=86400` (24 hours).\n\n---\n\n### Phase 7: Todo CRUD API Routes (Protected)\n\n**Step 7.1: Create todo API routes**\n\nFile: `/Users/flakerimi/TMP/todo/server/api/todos.dart`\n\n```dart\nimport 'package:duxt/duxt.dart';\nimport 'package:duxt_orm/duxt_orm.dart';\nimport '../../lib/models/todo.dart';\nimport '../../lib/models/user.dart';\nimport '../middleware/auth_middleware.dart';\n\nvoid registerTodoApi(DuxtServer server) {\n  // Helper: apply auth middleware and return the user, or null if unauthorized\n  Future<User?> authenticate(Request req) async {\n    final result = await authMiddleware(req);\n    if (result != null) return null;\n    return req.context['user'] as User;\n  }\n\n  // GET /api/todos - List all todos for the authenticated user\n  server.get('/api/todos', (req) async {\n    final authResult = await authMiddleware(req);\n    if (authResult != null) return authResult;\n\n    final user = req.context['user'] as User;\n    final todos = Model<Todo>(Todo());\n    final userTodos = await todos.where({'user_id': user.id}).get();\n\n    return Response.json({\n      'todos': userTodos.map((t) => t.toMap()).toList(),\n    });\n  });\n\n  // POST /api/todos - Create a new todo\n  server.post('/api/todos', (req) async {\n    final authResult = await authMiddleware(req);\n    if (authResult != null) return authResult;\n\n    final user = req.context['user'] as User;\n    final body = await req.body();\n\n    final title = body['title'] as String?;\n    if (title == null || title.isEmpty) {\n      return Response.json(\n        {'error': 'Title is required'},\n        status: 400,\n      );\n    }\n\n    final todos = Model<Todo>(Todo());\n    final todo = await todos.create({\n      'title': title,\n      'completed': false,\n      'user_id': user.id,\n    });\n\n    return Response.json(\n      {'message': 'Todo created', 'todo': todo.toMap()},\n      status: 201,\n    );\n  });\n\n  // GET /api/todos/:id - Get a specific todo\n  server.get('/api/todos/:id', (req) async {\n    final authResult = await authMiddleware(req);\n    if (authResult != null) return authResult;\n\n    final user = req.context['user'] as User;\n    final id = int.tryParse(req.params['id'] ?? '');\n\n    if (id == null) {\n      return Response.json({'error': 'Invalid todo ID'}, status: 400);\n    }\n\n    final todos = Model<Todo>(Todo());\n    final todo = await todos.find(id);\n\n    if (todo == null) {\n      return Response.json({'error': 'Todo not found'}, status: 404);\n    }\n\n    // Ownership check\n    if (todo.userId != user.id) {\n      return Response.json({'error': 'Todo not found'}, status: 404);\n    }\n\n    return Response.json({'todo': todo.toMap()});\n  });\n\n  // PUT /api/todos/:id - Update a todo\n  server.put('/api/todos/:id', (req) async {\n    final authResult = await authMiddleware(req);\n    if (authResult != null) return authResult;\n\n    final user = req.context['user'] as User;\n    final id = int.tryParse(req.params['id'] ?? '');\n\n    if (id == null) {\n      return Response.json({'error': 'Invalid todo ID'}, status: 400);\n    }\n\n    final todos = Model<Todo>(Todo());\n    final todo = await todos.find(id);\n\n    if (todo == null || todo.userId != user.id) {\n      return Response.json({'error': 'Todo not found'}, status: 404);\n    }\n\n    final body = await req.body();\n    final updateData = <String, dynamic>{};\n\n    if (body.containsKey('title')) {\n      updateData['title'] = body['title'];\n    }\n    if (body.containsKey('completed')) {\n      updateData['completed'] = body['completed'];\n    }\n\n    final updated = await todos.update(id, updateData);\n\n    return Response.json({\n      'message': 'Todo updated',\n      'todo': updated.toMap(),\n    });\n  });\n\n  // DELETE /api/todos/:id - Delete a todo\n  server.delete('/api/todos/:id', (req) async {\n    final authResult = await authMiddleware(req);\n    if (authResult != null) return authResult;\n\n    final user = req.context['user'] as User;\n    final id = int.tryParse(req.params['id'] ?? '');\n\n    if (id == null) {\n      return Response.json({'error': 'Invalid todo ID'}, status: 400);\n    }\n\n    final todos = Model<Todo>(Todo());\n    final todo = await todos.find(id);\n\n    if (todo == null || todo.userId != user.id) {\n      return Response.json({'error': 'Todo not found'}, status: 404);\n    }\n\n    await todos.delete(id);\n\n    return Response.json({'message': 'Todo deleted'});\n  });\n}\n```\n\nKey design decisions for Todo routes:\n- **Per-user isolation**: Every query filters by `user_id`. When a user tries to access another user's todo, the response is 404 (not 403) to avoid leaking information about the existence of resources.\n- **Auth middleware applied to every route**: Each handler calls `authMiddleware(req)` first. If it returns a non-null value (a 401 Response), the handler returns that immediately.\n- **Partial updates**: The PUT handler only updates fields that are present in the request body, allowing partial updates.\n- **Input validation**: Title is required for creation; ID is validated as a parseable integer.\n\n---\n\n### Phase 8: Server Entry Point\n\n**Step 8.1: Wire everything together in server/main.dart**\n\nFile: `/Users/flakerimi/TMP/todo/server/main.dart`\n\n```dart\nimport 'package:duxt/duxt.dart';\nimport 'api/auth.dart';\nimport 'api/todos.dart';\n\nvoid main() async {\n  final server = DuxtServer();\n\n  // Register API routes\n  registerAuthApi(server);\n  registerTodoApi(server);\n\n  // Start the server\n  await server.start();\n}\n```\n\nThis is the standard Duxt server entry point pattern. The `DuxtServer` handles:\n- Database initialization and auto-migration (from registered models)\n- Built-in security features (CSRF, rate limiting from Duxt's security layer)\n- Starting the HTTP server\n\n---\n\n### Phase 9: Project Configuration\n\n**Step 9.1: Verify duxt.yaml**\n\nFile: `/Users/flakerimi/TMP/todo/duxt.yaml`\n\nShould contain (set by `duxt create --mode=server`):\n```yaml\nmode: server\n```\n\n**Step 9.2: Database configuration**\n\nFile: `/Users/flakerimi/TMP/todo/duxt.config.dart`\n\nThe default configuration uses SQLite for development, which is sufficient:\n```dart\nclass DuxtConfig {\n  static const database = (\n    driver: String.fromEnvironment('DB_DRIVER', defaultValue: 'sqlite'),\n    host: String.fromEnvironment('DB_HOST', defaultValue: 'localhost'),\n    port: int.fromEnvironment('DB_PORT', defaultValue: 3306),\n    name: String.fromEnvironment('DB_NAME', defaultValue: 'todo'),\n    username: String.fromEnvironment('DB_USER', defaultValue: 'root'),\n    password: String.fromEnvironment('DB_PASS', defaultValue: ''),\n  );\n}\n```\n\nThe SQLite database file will be auto-created at `database/database.sqlite`. Tables for `users`, `todos`, and `sessions` will be auto-migrated by Duxt ORM when the server starts.\n\n---\n\n### Complete File Tree\n\n```\n/Users/flakerimi/TMP/todo/\n├── pubspec.yaml                          # Add dbcrypt, uuid deps\n├── duxt.yaml                             # mode: server (generated)\n├── duxt.config.dart                      # Database config (generated)\n├── lib/\n│   ├── main.dart                         # (generated by CLI)\n│   ├── app.dart                          # (generated by CLI)\n│   ├── models/\n│   │   ├── user