            "text": "<system-reminder>\nAs you answer the user's questions, you can use the following context:\n# claudeMd\nCodebase and user instructions are shown below. Be sure to adhere to these instructions. IMPORTANT: These instructions OVERRIDE any default behavior and you MUST follow them exactly as written.\n\nContents of /Users/flakerimi/.claude/CLAUDE.md (user's private global instructions for all projects):\n\n# NEVER add Co-Authored-By to commits. No co-author lines from Claude, Codex, or any AI. Ever.\n# NEVER, EVER delete any thing without confiming, even if BYPASSED PERMISSIONS is on. NEVER. NEVER.\n# ALWAYS confirm with the user before deleting any thing.\n# If the user requests deletion of files or data, ALWAYS confirm the request explicitly.\n# ALWAS TELL THE USER that this is NOT git repository, so if we delete files, they will be permanently deleted.\n# ALWAYS ask user if they want to create a git repo and commit to GitHub before making significant changes, so we don't lose work.\n\n# BEFORE any rm/delete command:\n# - ALWAYS run `ls` first to see what actually exists in the directory\n# - NEVER assume a directory is empty, even if you think you just created it\n# - Show the user what will be deleted and get explicit confirmation\n\n# BEFORE creating a directory or project:\n# - ALWAYS check if a directory with that name already exists using `ls`\n# - If it exists, ask the user what to do - DO NOT overwrite or delete\n\n# When instructions are ambiguous (like \"run from X\" or \"use X\"):\n# - ASK for clarification before taking destructive action\n# - Never guess - destructive actions are irreversible\n\n# NEVER chain rm with other commands (like `rm -rf X && mkdir Y`)\n# - Do them separately so each step can be verified\n\n# Instead of `rm`, use `trash` command - moves files to user trash folder instead of permanent deletion\n# - `trash file.txt` instead of `rm file.txt`\n# - `trash -r directory` instead of `rm -rf directory`\n# - This allows recovery from the system Trash if needed\n\n# NEVER dismiss warnings/errors as \"pre-existing\" or \"not from our changes\".\n# ALWAYS fix ALL warnings and errors you encounter, regardless of whether you introduced them.\n# No excuses - just fix them.\n\n# BEFORE running release, deploy, build, or any repetitive workflow:\n# - ALWAYS check for existing .sh scripts first (release.sh, deploy.sh, build.sh, etc.)\n# - Use `ls *.sh` or `glob **/*.sh` in the project root\n# - If a script exists for the task, USE IT instead of doing steps manually\n# - Scripts contain the correct sequence of steps (version bumps, changelog, tagging, etc.)\n# - Doing it manually risks missing steps (like updating version.dart)\n\n# NEVER invent fictional URLs, repos, links, or external references.\n# ALWAYS verify that URLs and external resources actually exist BEFORE using them.\n# If you don't have a verified URL, ask the user or mark it as placeholder/coming soon.\n# currentDate\nToday's date is 2026-02-23.\n\n      IMPORTANT: this context may or may not be relevant to your tasks. You should not respond to this context unless it is highly relevant to your task.\n</system-reminder>\n"
