            "type": "text",
            "text": "Base directory for this skill: /Users/flakerimi/.claude/skills/duxt\n\n# Duxt Framework Skill\n\nUse this skill when working with any Duxt package: duxt, duxt_orm, duxt_html, duxt_signals, or duxt_ui.\n\n## Ecosystem Overview\n\nDuxt is a meta-framework for Jaspr (Flutter for web). The stack:\n\n| Package | Version | Purpose |\n|---------|---------|---------|\n| **duxt** | 0.5.0 | Meta-framework: CLI, server, router, builder |\n| **duxt_orm** | 0.4.0 | ActiveRecord ORM with PostgreSQL/MySQL/SQLite |\n| **duxt_html** | 1.0.0 | 117 PascalCase HTML components for Jaspr |\n| **duxt_signals** | 0.1.2 | Reactive state: Signal, Computed, Effect, FormField |\n| **duxt_ui** | 0.3.1 | 80+ pre-built styled components (Tailwind CSS) |\n\n**Component layering:** `duxt_ui -> duxt_html -> jaspr`\n\nAll packages at `/Volumes/External/Duxt/` under `github.com/duxt-base/` org.\n\n---\n\n## duxt (v0.5.0) - Main Framework\n\n### CLI Commands\n\n```\nduxt create <name>          # New project (--mode, --template)\nduxt dev [--port=4000]      # Dev server with hot reload\nduxt build [--target]       # Production build (cross-compile supported)\nduxt start [--port]         # Production server\nduxt preview [--port=4000]  # Preview built project\nduxt generate               # Generate static site (SSG)\nduxt g <type> <name>        # Generator: module, page, component, model, api, layout\nduxt scaffold <name> [fields] # Full CRUD module with pages, model, API\nduxt d <type> <name>        # Delete generated resources\nduxt clean                  # Remove build artifacts\nduxt info                   # Project information\nduxt doctor                 # Environment diagnostics\nduxt update                 # Update CLI\nduxt docs generate          # Generate API docs\n```\n\n### Project Templates\n\n| Template | Purpose | Default Mode |\n|----------|---------|--------------|\n| **default** | Full-featured demo | static |\n| **minimal** | Clean starting point | static |\n| **html** | duxt_html + duxt_signals showcase | static |\n| **marketing** | Landing page with hero, features, pricing | static |\n| **blog** | Blog with categories, tags, ORM | server |\n| **saas** | SaaS with auth, dashboard, billing | server |\n\n### Rendering Modes\n\n- **static** (SSG) - Pre-renders at build time. Marketing sites, docs.\n- **server** (SSR) - Renders per request. Database-driven content.\n- **client** (SPA) - Client-side only (coming soon).\n\n### DuxtServer\n\n```dart\nimport 'package:duxt/server.dart';\n\nfinal server = DuxtServer(\n  port: 3000,\n  apiDir: 'server/api',\n  staticDir: '.output/public',\n  middleware: [...],\n  requestTimeout: Duration(seconds: 30),\n);\n\n// HTTP methods\nserver.get('/api/users', handler);\nserver.post('/api/users', handler);\nserver.put('/api/users/:id', handler);\nserver.delete('/api/users/:id', handler);\nserver.patch('/api/users/:id', handler);\nserver.all('/api/health', handler);\nserver.use('/api/posts', PostsApiHandler());\n```\n\n### Middleware\n\n```dart\n// Built-in middleware\ncors(origins: ['http://localhost:3000'], methods: ['GET', 'POST'], headers: ['Content-Type', 'Authorization'])\nsecurityHeaders()       // X-Content-Type-Options, X-Frame-Options, X-XSS-Protection\nbodyLimit(maxSize: 1024 * 1024)  // 1MB default\nrateLimit(maxRequests: 100, window: Duration(minutes: 1))\ntimeout(duration: Duration(seconds: 30))\njsonBody()              // Parse JSON bodies\nlogger()                // Request logging with timing\nauth(verifier)          // Custom auth verification\ncsrf()                  // CSRF token validation\n```\n\n### API Handler Pattern\n\n```dart\nclass PostsHandler extends ApiHandler {\n  Future<ApiResponse> get(ApiRequest request) async { ... }\n  Future<ApiResponse> post(ApiRequest request) async { ... }\n  Future<ApiResponse> put(ApiRequest request) async { ... }\n  Future<ApiResponse> delete(ApiRequest request) async { ... }\n}\n\n// ApiRequest properties\nrequest.method       // HTTP method\nrequest.path         // Request path\nrequest.params       // Route params {:id}\nrequest.param('id')  // Single param\nrequest.query('q')   // Query parameter\nrequest.body         // Raw body string\nrequest.json         // Parsed JSON body\nrequest.headers      // Request headers\n\n// ApiResponse factories\nApiResponse.ok(data)\nApiResponse.created(data)\nApiResponse.noContent()\nApiResponse.badRequest('message')\nApiResponse.unauthorized('message')\nApiResponse.forbidden('message')\nApiResponse.notFound('message')\nApiResponse.methodNotAllowed()\nApiResponse.error('message')\nApiResponse.redirect('/path')\n```\n\n### File-Based Routing\n\n```\nlib/home/pages/index.dart          -> /\nlib/blog/pages/index.dart          -> /blog\nlib/blog/pages/_id_.dart           -> /blog/:id\nlib/blog/pages/new.dart            -> /blog/new\nlib/blog/pages/_id_/edit.dart      -> /blog/:id/edit\nlib/blog/content/getting-started.md -> /blog/getting-started\n```\n\n### Navigation API\n\n```dart\nuseRouter()               // Get router instance\ncontext.push('/path')     // Navigate forward\ncontext.replace('/path')  // Replace current route\ncontext.back()            // Go back\ncontext.pushNamed('name') // Named route\ncontext.preload('/path')  // Preload route\n```\n\n### Error Pages\n\n```dart\n// Component-based (Jaspr)\nRouter(errorBuilder: DuxtErrorPage.routerErrorBuilder)\n\n// Static HTML (server fallback)\nDuxtErrorHtml.notFound(path)    // 404 page\nDuxtErrorHtml.serverError()     // 500 page\n```\n\n### Environment Variables (Server Mode)\n\n```\nPORT=3001              # Server port\nDATA_DIR=.             # SQLite database location\nDB_DRIVER=postgres     # Database driver\nDB_HOST, DB_PORT, DB_NAME, DB_USER, DB_PASS  # DB connection\n```\n\n---\n\n## duxt_orm (v0.4.0) - ActiveRecord ORM\n\n### Setup\n\n```dart\nimport 'package:duxt_orm/duxt_orm.dart';\n\nawait DuxtOrm.init((\n  driver: 'sqlite',\n  database: 'app.db',\n  path: '${Platform.environment['DATA_DIR'] ?? '.'}/app.db',\n  host: '', port: 0, username: '', password: '', ssl: false,\n));\n\n// Register models before migrate\nUser.register();\nPost.register();\n\nawait DuxtOrm.migrate();\n```\n\n### Model Definition\n\n```dart\nclass User extends Entity {\n  int? _id;\n  String? email;\n  String? name;\n\n  User({int? id, this.email, this.name}) : _id = id;\n\n  @override\n  dynamic get id => _id;\n  @override\n  set id(dynamic value) => _id = value as int?;\n\n  @override\n  Map<String, dynamic> toMap() => {'email': email, 'name': name};\n\n  factory User.fromRow(Map<String, dynamic> row) => User(\n    id: row['id'] as int?,\n    email: row['email'] as String?,\n    name: row['name'] as String?,\n  );\n\n  // Relations (access loaded data)\n  List<Post> get posts => getRelation<List<Post>>('posts') ?? [];\n\n  static void register() {\n    Entity.registerModel<User>(User.fromRow, schema: {\n      'id': Column.integer().primaryKey().autoIncrement(),\n      'email': Column.string().notNull().unique(),\n      'name': Column.string(100).nullable(),\n    });\n    Entity.registerRelation<User>('posts', HasMany<Post>(foreignKey: 'user_id'));\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### CRUD Operations\n\n```dart\nfinal users = Model<User>();\n\n// Create\nfinal user = await users.create({'email': 'a@b.com', 'name': 'Alice'});\n\n// Read\nfinal all = await users.all();\nfinal user = await users.find(1);\nfinal user = await users.findOrFail(1);  // throws RecordNotFoundException\nfinal first = await users.first();\n\n// Update\nawait user.update({'name': 'Bob'});\n\n// Delete\nawait user.destroy();       // Soft delete (sets deleted_at)\nawait user.forceDelete();   // Permanent delete\nawait user.restore();       // Restore soft-deleted\n```\n\n### Query Builder\n\n```dart\nfinal results = await Model<User>().query()\n  .select(['id', 'email', 'name'])\n  .where('email', 'a@b.com')\n  .orWhere('name', 'Alice')\n  .whereNull('deleted_at')\n  .whereNotNull('email')\n  .whereIn('id', [1, 2, 3])\n  .whereNotIn('status', ['banned'])\n  .whereBetween('age', 18, 65)\n  .whereLike('name', '%alice%')\n  .whereRaw('LENGTH(name) > ?', [3])\n  .orderBy('created_at', 'DESC')\n  .orderByDesc('name')\n  .latest()                   // ORDER BY created_at DESC\n  .oldest()                   // ORDER BY created_at ASC\n  .limit(10)\n  .offset(20)\n  .distinct()\n  .groupBy('status')\n  .having('COUNT(*) > 1')\n  .join('profiles', 'users.id', '=', 'profiles.user_id')\n  .leftJoin('orders', 'users.id', '=', 'orders.user_id')\n  .get();\n\n// Aggregates\nawait query.count();\nawait query.sum('amount');\nawait query.avg('rating');\nawait query.max('price');\nawait query.min('price');\nawait query.exists();\nawait query.doesntExist();\nawait query.pluck('email');   // List<dynamic> of single column\n\n// Bulk operations\nawait query.update({'status': 'active'});\nawait query.delete();\nawait query.forceDelete();\nawait query.restore();\nawait query.increment('views');\nawait query.decrement('stock', 5);\n\n// Debug\nprint(query.toSql());\n\n// Raw SQL\nawait DuxtOrm.raw('SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?', [1]);\nawait DuxtOrm.execute('DELETE FROM sessions');\n\n// Transactions\nawait DuxtOrm.transaction((tx) async {\n  await tx.query('UPDATE accounts SET balance = balance - 100 WHERE id = ?', [1]);\n  await tx.query('UPDATE accounts SET balance = balance + 100 WHERE id = ?', [2]);\n});\n```\n\n### Relations\n\n```dart\n// HasMany - one-to-many\nEntity.registerRelation<User>('posts', HasMany<Post>(foreignKey: 'user_id'));\n\n// BelongsTo - many-to-one\nEntity.registerRelation<Post>('author', BelongsTo<User>(foreignKey: 'user_id'));\n\n// HasOne - one-to-one\nEntity.registerRelation<User>('profile', HasOne<Profile>(foreignKey: 'user_id'));\n\n// BelongsToMany - many-to-many (pivot table)\nEntity.registerRelation<Post>('tags', BelongsToMany<Tag>(\n  pivotTable: 'post_tags',\n  foreignPivotKey: 'post_id',\n  relatedPivotKey: 'tag_id',\n));\nEntity.registerPivotTable('post_tags', schema: {\n  'post_id': Column.integer().notNull().references('posts'),\n  'tag_id': Column.integer().notNull().references('tags'),\n}, primaryKey: ['post_id', 'tag_id']);\n\n// Eager loading (prevents N+1)\nfinal posts = await Model<Post>().include(['author', 'tags', 'author.profile']).all();\n\n// Pivot table operations\nawait post.attach('tags', tagId);\nawait post.detach('tags', tagId);\nawait post.sync('tags', [1, 2, 3]);\n```\n\n### Schema Column Types\n\n```dart\nColumn.integer()             Column.bigInteger()        Column.smallInteger()\nColumn.string([length=255])  Column.text()              Column.boolean()\nColumn.date()                Column.time()              Column.dateTime()\nColumn.decimal([p=10, s=2])  Column.float()             Column.double_()\nColumn.json()                Column.binary()\n\n// Modifiers (chainable)\n.primaryKey()  .autoIncrement()  .notNull()  .nullable()\n.unique()      .defaultValue(v)  .references('table', 'col')\n.onDelete('CASCADE')  .onUpdate('SET NULL')\n```\n\n### Soft Deletes & Timestamps\n\n- Soft deletes: enabled by default. Uses `deleted_at` column.\n- Timestamps: enabled by default. Auto-manages `created_at`/`updated_at`.\n- `withTrashed()` / `onlyTrashed()` scopes for queries.\n- Override: `softDeletes = false` or `timestamps = false` in Entity.\n\n### Supported Drivers\n\n| Driver | Package | Placeholder | Escape |\n|--------|---------|------------|--------|\n| PostgreSQL | `postgres` v3.0.0 | `API, cookies` | `\"` |\n| MySQL | `mysql_client` v0.0.27 | `:p0, :p1` | `` ` `` |\n| SQLite | `sqlite3` v2.4.0 | `?` | `\"` |\n\n---\n\n## duxt_html (v1.0.0) - 117 HTML Components\n\n### Import\n\n```dart\nimport 'package:duxt_html/duxt_html.dart';\n```\n\n### Component API Pattern\n\nEvery component follows the same signature pattern:\n\n```dart\nComponent Div({\n  String? className,     // CSS classes (Tailwind etc.)\n  String? style,         // Inline CSS string\n  String? id,            // Element ID\n  Component? child,      // Single child\n  List<Component>? children,  // Multiple children\n  Map<String, String>? attributes,  // Extra HTML attributes\n  Map<String, EventCallback>? events,  // Event handlers\n  Key? key,\n})\n```\n\n### All 117 Components by Category\n\n**Document (10):** Html, Head, Body, Title, Meta, HtmlLink, Base, StyleElement, Script, Noscript\n\n**Content (15):** Div, P, Hr, Pre, Blockquote, Ul, Ol, Li, Dl, Dt, Dd, Menu, Figure, Figcaption\n\n**Headings (6):** H1, H2, H3, H4, H5, H6\n\n**Text (21):** A, Span, B, Strong, Em, I, Small, Mark, Del, Ins, Sub, Sup, S, Abbr, Cite, Code, Dfn, Kbd, Samp, HtmlVar, Wbr, Bdo, Br, Bdi, Q, Ruby, Rt, Rp, Time, HtmlData\n\n**Forms (15):** Form, Input, Button, Label, Fieldset, Legend, Textarea, Select, Option, Optgroup, Datalist, Output, Meter, Progress\n\n**Table (10):** Table, Thead, Tbody, Tfoot, Tr, Th, Td, Caption, Colgroup, Col\n\n**Media (15):** Img, Picture, Source, Audio, Video, Track, ImageMap, Area, Canvas, Iframe, Embed, ObjectEmbed, Script, Figure, Figcaption\n\n**Semantic (7):** Header, Footer, Nav, Main, Article, Aside, Section, Address, Details, Summary, Dialog\n\n**SVG (12):** Svg, G, Path, Circle, Rect, Line, Polyline, Polygon, SvgText, Tspan, Defs, Use\n\n**Web Components:** Slot, HtmlTemplate, HtmlData\n\n### Helpers\n\n```dart\nText('Hello')                      // Text node\nRaw('<b>Bold</b>')                 // Raw HTML (XSS warning!)\nFragment([child1, child2])         // Fragment wrapper\nresolveChildren(child, children)   // Resolve child/children\nparseStyles('color: red')         // Parse CSS string to Styles\n```\n\n### Naming Conventions (Dart Conflicts)\n\n| HTML Element | duxt_html Name | Reason |\n|-------------|---------------|--------|\n| `<link>` | `HtmlLink` | Conflicts with Material Link |\n| `<object>` | `ObjectEmbed` | Conflicts with Dart Object |\n| `<map>` | `ImageMap` | Conflicts with Dart Map |\n| `<var>` | `HtmlVar` | Conflicts with Dart var |\n| `<style>` | `StyleElement` | Conflicts with Styles type |\n| `<template>` | `HtmlTemplate` | Conflicts with Dart Template |\n| `<data>` | `HtmlData` | Conflicts with common variable names |\n\n### Important Notes\n\n- `RawText` must be imported separately: `import 'package:jaspr/dom.dart' show RawText;`\n- When using with `jaspr/jaspr.dart`, add `hide Text` to avoid ambiguous import: `import 'package:jaspr/jaspr.dart' hide Text;`\n- Input/Button types are strings: `Input(type: 'text')`, `Button(type: 'button')`\n- Form has no `onSubmit` - use `events: {'submit': handler}`\n\n---\n\n## duxt_signals (v0.1.2) - Reactive State\n\n### Import\n\n```dart\nimport 'package:duxt_signals/duxt_signals.dart';\n```\n\n### Signal (Mutable Reactive Value)\n\n```dart\nfinal count = signal(0);\n\ncount()              // Read value (call syntax)\ncount.value          // Read value (property)\ncount.set(5)         // Set value\ncount.update((v) => v + 1)  // Update with function\ncount.listen((v) { })       // Subscribe to changes\n```\n\n### Computed (Derived Reactive Value)\n\n```dart\nfinal firstName = signal('John');\nfinal lastName = signal('Doe');\nfinal fullName = computed(() => '${firstName()} ${lastName()}');\n// Auto-tracks dependencies, recomputes when they change\n```\n\n### Effect (Side Effects)\n\n```dart\nfinal dispose = effect(() {\n  print('Count changed: ${count()}');  // Runs when count changes\n});\ndispose();  // Stop effect\n```\n\n### Batch Updates\n\n```dart\nbatch(() {\n  signal1.set(value1);\n  signal2.set(value2);\n});  // Notifications deferred until batch completes\n```\n\n### SignalState (Auto-Tracking Component)\n\n```dart\nclass MyComponent extends SignalState<MyComponent> {\n  final count = signal(0);\n\n  @override\n  Component buildComponent() {\n    // Signals read here are auto-tracked\n    return Div(children: [Text('Count: ${count()}')]);\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### FormField (Signal + Validation)\n\n```dart\nfinal email = formField('', validators: [\n  required('Email is required'),\n  email('Invalid email format'),\n]);\n\nemail()            // Current value\nemail.touched      // Has been focused/blurred\nemail.dirty        // Changed from initial\nemail.error        // Validation error message (String?)\nemail.isValid      // No errors\nemail.hasError     // Has errors\n\nemail.set('new@email.com')  // Set and validate\nemail.touch()               // Mark as touched\nemail.reset()               // Reset to initial\nemail.validate()            // Manual validation\n```\n\n### Built-in Validators\n\n```dart\nrequired('Required')              // String not empty\nrequiredValue<T>('Required')      // Value not null\nminLength(3, 'Too short')         // Min string length\nmaxLength(100, 'Too long')        // Max string length\nemail('Invalid email')            // Email format\npattern(RegExp(r'...'), 'Invalid') // Regex match\nmin(0, 'Must be >= 0')            // Number minimum\nmax(100, 'Must be <= 100')        // Number maximum\nnotEmpty<T>('List empty')         // List not empty\n```\n\n### Important Notes\n\n- Avoid naming variables `email` or `form` - they shadow the `email()` validator and jaspr's `form()` function.\n- Input blur events: use `events: {'blur': (_) => field.touch()}` not `onBlur`.\n\n---\n\n## duxt_ui (v0.3.1) - Styled Components\n\n### Import\n\n```dart\nimport 'package:duxt_ui/duxt_ui.dart';\n```\n\nAll components use `D` prefix to avoid conflicts with duxt_html.\n\n### Component Categories\n\n**Core (11):** DButton, DInput, DCard, DBadge, DAlert, DModal, DDropdown, DTabs, DTable, DAvatar, DSpinner\n\n**Form (11):** DForm, DFormField, DCheckbox, DCheckboxGroup, DRadioGroup, DSwitch, DSelect, DSlider, DInputNumber, DPinInput, DFileUpload\n\n**Layout (5):** DContainer, DSeparator, DMain, DHeader, DFooter\n\n**Navigation (4):** DBreadcrumb, DNavigationMenu, DLink, DKbd\n\n**Overlay (6):** DOverlay, DSlideover, DPopover, DContextMenu, DTooltip, DDrawer\n\n**Content (5):** DAccordion, DCollapsible, DSkeleton, DEmpty, DError\n\n**Dashboard (9):** DDashboard, DDashboardGroup, DDashboardPanel, DDashboardNavbar, DDashboardSidebar, DDashboardSidebarToggle, DDashboardSidebarCollapse, DDashboardToolbar, DDashboardSearch\n\n**Data (7):** DChip, DAvatarGroup, DPagination, DProgress, DTimeline, DTree, DUser\n\n**Feedback (3):** DToast, DToaster, DBanner\n\n**Page (10):** DPage, DPageBody, DPageHeader, DPageHero, DPageSection, DPageAside, DPageCard, DPageGrid, DPageColumns, DPageCTA\n\n**Blog (2):** DBlogPost, DBlogPosts\n\n**Pricing (3):** DPricingPlan, DPricingPlans, DPricingTable\n\n**Chat (5):** DChatMessage, DChatMessages, DChatPrompt, DChatPromptSubmit, DChatPalette\n\n**Utility (6):** DIcon, DCarousel, DMarquee, DScrollArea, DStepper, DCalendar\n\n### Theme System\n\n```dart\n// Colors\nDColor.primary    // cyan\nDColor.secondary  // blue\nDColor.success    // green\nDColor.info       // sky\nDColor.warning    // yellow\nDColor.error      // red\nDColor.neutral    // slate\n\n// Semantic text colors\nDTextColors.highlighted  DTextColors.muted  DTextColors.dimmed  DTextColors.inverted\n\n// Background colors\nDBgColors.defaultBg  DBgColors.elevated  DBgColors.inverted  DBgColors.muted\n\n// Sizes\nDSize.xs  DSize.sm  DSize.md  DSize.lg  DSize.xl\n\n// Variants\nDVariant.solid  DVariant.outline  DVariant.soft  DVariant.subtle  DVariant.ghost  DVariant.link\n```\n\n### Component Examples\n\n```dart\n// Button\nDButton(\n  label: 'Click me',\n  variant: DButtonVariant.solid,\n  color: DColor.primary,\n  size: DSize.md,\n  loading: false,\n  disabled: false,\n  onClick: () { },\n)\n\n// Input\nDInput(\n  value: '',\n  placeholder: 'Enter text',\n  variant: DInputVariant.outline,\n  size: DSize.md,\n  error: null,\n  onInput: (value) { },\n)\n\n// Card\nDCard(\n  variant: DCardVariant.outline,\n  children: [\n    DCardHeader(title: 'Title', description: 'Desc'),\n    DCardBody(children: [...]),\n    DCardFooter(children: [...]),\n  ],\n)\n\n// Modal (no @client needed)\nDModal(\n  trigger: DButton(label: 'Open'),\n  title: 'Confirm',\n  description: 'Are you sure?',\n  children: [...],\n)\n\n// Table\nDTable<User>(\n  data: users,\n  columns: [\n    DTableColumn(label: 'Name', value: (u) => u.name),\n    DTableColumn(label: 'Email', value: (u) => u.email),\n  ],\n)\n```\n\n### Interactive Components (No @client Needed)\n\nThese work without client-side Dart annotation using native HTML:\n- DDropdown - `<details>/<summary>` + JS\n- DPopover - `<details>/<summary>` + JS\n- DCollapsible - native `<details>/<summary>`\n- DAccordion - native `<details>` with `name` attribute\n- DModal/DSlideover/DDrawer - native `<dialog>` element\n- DCarousel - inline JS\n- DCalendar - inline JS with form integration\n- DPinInput - auto-advance JS\n- DInputNumber - increment/decrement buttons\n\n### Controlled Variants (Need @client)\n\n- DModalControlled - state-controlled modal\n- DSlideoverControlled - state-controlled slideover\n- DDrawerControlled - state-controlled drawer\n\n---\n\n## Common Patterns\n\n### File Structure Convention\n\n```\nlib/\n  home/\n    pages/index.dart       # Home page (/)\n    components/            # Module components\n    content/               # Markdown content\n  blog/\n    pages/\n      index.dart           # /blog\n      _id_.dart            # /blog/:id\n      new.dart             # /blog/new\n  .generated/\n    routes.dart            # Auto-generated routes\nlayouts/\n  default.dart             # Default layout\n  error.dart               # Error layout\nserver/\n  main.dart                # Server entry point\n  api/                     # API handlers\npublic/                    # Static files\n```\n\n### Typical Server Setup\n\n```dart\nimport 'package:duxt/server.dart';\nimport 'package:duxt_orm/duxt_orm.dart';\n\nvoid main() async {\n  await DuxtOrm.init(dbConfig);\n  User.register();\n  Post.register();\n  await DuxtOrm.migrate();\n\n  final server = DuxtServer(\n    port: int.parse(Platform.environment['PORT'] ?? '3001'),\n    apiDir: 'server/api',\n    staticDir: '.output/public',\n    middleware: [\n      securityHeaders(),\n      bodyLimit(),\n      cors(origins: ['http://localhost:4000']),\n      jsonBody(),\n      logger(),\n    ],\n  );\n\n  server.get('/api/posts', (req) async {\n    final posts = await Model<Post>().include(['author']).all();\n    return json(posts.map((p) => p.toMap()).toList());\n  });\n\n  await server.start();\n}\n```\n\n### Versioning Rules\n\n- Use **patch increments** (0.x.1, 0.x.2) for feature additions\n- Only bump minor/major for genuinely breaking changes\n\n### Code Style Notes\n\n- duxt_html uses PascalCase functions returning Component\n- duxt_ui uses D-prefixed classes extending StatelessComponent/StatefulComponent\n- Tailwind CSS for all styling\n- `cx([...])` utility for conditional class merging (like clsx)\n- Code blocks in duxt_docs markdown must NOT use language tags (no ```dart) - causes crashes\n"
