  "response_text": "Based on the search results, here's what I found about the latest version of Express.js as of 2026:\n\nThe latest version is 5.2.1, which was last published 3 months ago. However, Express 5.1.0 is now the default on npm.\n\nExpress version 5 was released in October 2024 after ten years of development. This version focuses on simplifying the codebase, improving security, and dropping support for older Node.js versions to enable better performance and maintainability.\n\nKey features of Express 5 include:\n- Dropped support for Node.js versions before v18\n- Middleware can now return rejected promises, caught by the router as errors\n- Removed old, deprecated API method signatures from Express v3/v4\n\nLooking ahead, the next version of Express, version 6, will focus on performance, modernization, and greater independence from Node's legacy HTTP internals.",
