            "content": "Web search results for query: \"JWT authentication Node.js best practices 2025 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"JWT Authentication In Node.js - GeeksforGeeks\",\"url\":\"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/node-js/jwt-authentication-with-node-js/\"},{\"title\":\"5 JWT authentication best practices for Node.js apps | Tech Tonic\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/deno-the-complete-reference/5-jwt-authentication-best-practices-for-node-js-apps-f1aaceda3f81\"},{\"title\":\"Node.js Express JWT Authentication with MySQL & Roles\",\"url\":\"https://www.corbado.com/blog/nodejs-express-mysql-jwt-authentication-roles\"},{\"title\":\"JWT Authentication in Node.js: A Practical Guide | by Dev Balaji | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://dvmhn07.medium.com/jwt-authentication-in-node-js-a-practical-guide-c8ab1b432a49\"},{\"title\":\"How to Secure JWT Authentication in a Node.js API? · community · Discussion #147581\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/orgs/community/discussions/147581\"},{\"title\":\"JWT Authentication in Node.js Explained with Secure Examples\",\"url\":\"https://nareshit.com/blogs/jwt-authentication-in-node-js\"},{\"title\":\"How to Use JWT and Node.js for Better App Security | Toptal®\",\"url\":\"https://www.toptal.com/developers/json/jwt-nodejs-security\"},{\"title\":\"Node.js API Authentication\",\"url\":\"https://www.w3schools.com/nodejs/nodejs_api_auth.asp\"},{\"title\":\"How to Implement JSON Web Token (JWT) Authentication in Node.js | Alex Rusin Blog\",\"url\":\"https://blog.alexrusin.com/how-to-implement-json-web-token-jwt-authentication-in-node-js/\"},{\"title\":\"Securing Your Node.js Applications in 2025: Best Practices for Authentication and Authorization | by habtesoft | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://habtesoft.medium.com/securing-your-node-js-applications-in-2025-best-practices-for-authentication-and-authorization-0bd574ae3bb3\"}]\n\nHere are the current best practices for JWT authentication in Node.js based on recent 2025-2026 sources:\n\n## Key JWT Best Practices\n\n### 1. **Secure Secret Key Management**\nNever hardcode your secret key in your code or store it in a publicly accessible location. Store your secure secret key securely, such as using environment variables or a reliable secrets manager.\n\n### 2. **Token Expiration Strategy**\nAccess tokens should have a short expiration time, typically between 15 minutes to 1 hour, as they are used to access protected routes and should be short-lived to minimize damage in case of token theft. Refresh tokens should have a longer expiration time, typically between 1 day to 1 week.\n\n### 3. **Refresh Token Rotation**\nUse Refresh Token Rotation: Every time a refresh token is used, issue a new one and invalidate the old one, which limits the risk if a token is compromised.\n\n### 4. **Token Storage**\nHTTP-Only Cookies cannot be accessed by JavaScript, are protected from XSS, can use Secure + SameSite policies, and are ideal for browser-based apps, making this the most secure storage method for web apps.\n\n### 5. **Token Revocation and Tracking**\nImplement a revoke mechanism: Maintain a server-side blacklist or a database to track active/invalidated tokens, and ensure refresh tokens have a longer expiration but are carefully monitored for misuse. Add a unique identifier (jti) to each JWT and track them in a server-side database to detect and prevent reuse of revoked tokens.\n\n### 6. **Enhanced Security Monitoring**\nRegularly update JWT libraries to ensure you're protected against known vulnerabilities.\n\nThese practices align with modern security standards for 2025-2026, emphasizing stateless authentication while maintaining robust server-side controls.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."
