            "content": "Web search results for query: \"JWT access token refresh token rotation pattern Node.js 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Auth.js | Refresh Token Rotation\",\"url\":\"https://authjs.dev/guides/refresh-token-rotation\"},{\"title\":\"Refresh Token Rotation: Best Practices for Developers\",\"url\":\"https://www.serverion.com/uncategorized/refresh-token-rotation-best-practices-for-developers/\"},{\"title\":\"Refresh Auth Token Rotation (Node js & React ) — Part 1 | by Tókos Bence | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@tokosbex/auth-token-rotation-node-js-react-part-1-b83a87d7fb4d\"},{\"title\":\"How to Build a Secure Authentication System with JWT and Refresh Tokens\",\"url\":\"https://www.freecodecamp.org/news/how-to-build-a-secure-authentication-system-with-jwt-and-refresh-tokens/\"},{\"title\":\"Refresh Token Rotation | NextAuth.js\",\"url\":\"https://next-auth.js.org/v3/tutorials/refresh-token-rotation\"},{\"title\":\"JWT Token Rotation and Reuse Detection - Aryan Shaw's blog\",\"url\":\"https://aryanshaw.hashnode.dev/jwt-token-rotation-and-reuse-detection\"},{\"title\":\"Secure Authentication with JWTs & Rotating Refresh Tokens (TypeScript + Express + Vanilla JS) - DEV Community\",\"url\":\"https://dev.to/wiljeder/secure-authentication-with-jwts-rotating-refresh-tokens-typescript-express-vanilla-js-4f41\"},{\"title\":\"JSON Web Tokens (JWT) & Refresh Tokens: The Complete Backend Guide | by tekeshwar singh | Dec, 2025 | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://tsvillain.medium.com/json-web-tokens-jwt-refresh-tokens-the-complete-backend-guide-271bdf0e7b49\"},{\"title\":\"JWT Authentication With Refresh Tokens - GeeksforGeeks\",\"url\":\"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/node-js/jwt-authentication-with-refresh-tokens/\"},{\"title\":\"**JWT Authentication Security Guide: Refresh Token Rotation and Production-Ready Implementation**\",\"url\":\"https://jsschools.com/web_dev/jwt-authentication-security-guide-refresh-token/\"}]\n\nI've found comprehensive information about JWT access token refresh token rotation patterns in Node.js. Here's what the search results show:\n\n## Overview\n\nRefresh token rotation is the practice of updating an access token on behalf of the user without requiring interaction (like re-authenticating).\n\n## Key Concepts\n\n**Token Expiration Strategy:**\nWhen a user logs in, the authorization server provides two tokens: a short-lived access token (valid for 15–60 minutes) and a longer-lived refresh token (lasting 7–14 days).\n\n**Rotation Approaches:**\nTime-based rotation automatically rotates tokens after a certain period—for example, a token may be valid for 24 hours and then automatically replaced with a new one. Usage-based rotation rotates tokens based on how often they are used—for example, a token may be valid for 100 requests and then automatically replaced with a new one.\n\n## Node.js Implementation Pattern\n\nA Node.js token rotation function generates a new access token and refresh token pair, invalidates the old refresh token, and stores metadata with a family ID and hash of the previous token.\n\n**Secure Storage:**\nStore a SHA-256 hash, not the raw token, so a database leak does not give attackers the actual token string.\n\nThe refresh token goes to an HTTP-only cookie scoped to /api/auth/refresh, keeping the refresh token away from frontend code while still letting the browser send it to the refresh endpoint.\n\n**Cookie Security Flags:**\nUse httpOnly: true, secure: true in production, sameSite: 'strict', and a narrow path such as /api/auth/refresh to reduce XSS and CSRF risk.\n\n## Security Best Practices\n\nDestroy the old refresh token and issue a new one to prevent replay attacks. Token reuse detection is a security mechanism used to detect and prevent the reuse of a previously issued token because if an attacker obtains a valid token, they can use it to gain unauthorized access unless the token is detected and invalidated.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.",
