  "response_text": "I've found comprehensive information about JWT token revocation blacklist strategies for Node.js. Here are the key findings:\n\n## JWT Blacklist Overview\n\nA JWT blacklist/deny list is a list of tokens that should no longer grant access to your system. Token blacklisting is a widely used method to revoke JWT tokens.\n\n## Core Implementation Strategy\n\nWhen your web-server receives a logout request, take the token and store it in an in-memory database, like Redis, because of speed and efficiency, as you don't want to hit your main database every time someone wants to logout. You could use a traditional database, but a much better approach is to use an in-memory data cache, like Redis.\n\n## Key Challenges\n\nThe statelessness of JWTs poses significant challenges when it comes to revocation. Unlike traditional session-based authentication, where sessions can be invalidated by removing them from the server, JWTs remain valid until their expiration (exp) time, which is embedded within the token's payload.\n\n## Alternative Strategies\n\n**Token Versioning**: Token versioning is a lightweight alternative to blacklisting. Instead of storing revoked tokens, you store a version number for each user. When you need to revoke all tokens, you simply increment the version.\n\n**Short-Lived Tokens with Refresh Tokens**: Instead of maintaining a blacklist, you can use very short-lived access tokens (5-15 minutes) combined with refresh tokens. When you need to revoke access, you simply stop accepting the refresh token.\n\n## Distributed Approach\n\nA more advanced approach, without a single point of failure, can be implemented with Kafka. Kafka is a distributed and reliable message log by nature. Consequently, a blacklist of revoked tokens can be stored in Kafka.\n\n## Best Practices\n\nWhether through token blacklisting, rotating secrets, or using refresh tokens, implementing a robust revocation strategy is essential to protecting your application and users' data.",
  "response_type": "stream",
  "response_status": 200
},
