  "response_text": "Based on the search results, here's what I found about these Node.js authentication libraries:\n\n## Arctic\nArctic is a collection of OAuth 2.0 clients for popular providers. It's light weight, fully-typed, runtime-agnostic, and built using oslo.\n\n## Oslo\nOslo provides simple, runtime agnostic, and fully-typed packages with minimal dependency for auth and cryptography. However, it's worth noting that the oslo package is no longer supported, with a successor project available at oslojs.dev.\n\n## Better Auth\nBetter Auth is described as the most comprehensive authentication library for TypeScript, with the latest version 1.3.27 published 3 days ago. There's significant momentum behind this library in 2025/2026.\n\n## Auth.js (Formerly NextAuth.js)\nAuth.js, formerly known as NextAuth.js, is now being maintained and overseen by the Better Auth team.\n\nThese libraries represent the current Node.js authentication ecosystem, with Better Auth emerging as a prominent comprehensive solution in 2025-2026, while Arctic focuses specifically on OAuth 2.0 integration.",
