  "response_text": "Based on my search results, I found general information about JWT authentication in Node.js, but the search did not return specific results about \"better-auth\" as a particular library or framework. The results cover JWT authentication concepts and implementations in Node.js generally.\n\nHere's what I found about JWT authentication features commonly used in Node.js applications in 2025:\n\n## JWT Authentication Features in Node.js\n\n**Core JWT Functionality:**\n- JWT is a compact, URL-safe token format that allows the server to verify a token without storing user state\n- A JWT consists of a header, payload, and signature, and only ensures integrity\n\n**Key Authentication Capabilities:**\n- Access tokens and refresh tokens serve different purposes: access tokens are short-lived for request authorization, while refresh tokens allow long-lived sessions without repeated logins\n- Token verification belongs in middleware, where Express can validate signatures, enforce expiration, and attach user claims to req.user for downstream authorization\n\n**Advantages for Modern Applications:**\n- JWTs enable stateless authentication, allowing servers to validate requests without maintaining session data, which fits well with distributed and horizontally scaled systems\n\n**Common Implementation Approach:**\n- JWT is typically created in Node.js using a library, most commonly jsonwebtoken\n\nIf you're looking for information specifically about a \"better-auth\" library, you may want to search for its official documentation directly, as it doesn't appear prominently in general JWT authentication resources.",
