            "content": "Web search results for query: \"arctic oslo auth.js better-auth Node.js authentication library 2025 2026\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Arctic v3 documentation\",\"url\":\"https://arcticjs.dev/\"},{\"title\":\"arctic - npm\",\"url\":\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/arctic/v/0.7.1\"},{\"title\":\"Lucia\",\"url\":\"https://lucia-auth.com/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - pilcrowonpaper/arctic: OAuth 2.0 clients for popular providers\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/pilcrowonpaper/arctic\"},{\"title\":\"Auth.js is now part of Better Auth | Better Auth\",\"url\":\"https://www.better-auth.com/blog/authjs-joins-better-auth\"},{\"title\":\"better-auth - npm\",\"url\":\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/better-auth/v/0.2.6-beta.4?activeTab=dependencies\"},{\"title\":\"Better Auth\",\"url\":\"https://www.better-auth.com/\"},{\"title\":\"Oslo documentation\",\"url\":\"https://oslo.js.org/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - lucia-auth/lucia: Authentication, simple and clean\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/lucia-auth/lucia\"},{\"title\":\"OAuth 2.0\",\"url\":\"https://arcticjs.dev/guides/oauth2\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's information about these Node.js authentication libraries:\n\n## Arctic\n\nArctic is a collection of OAuth 2.0 clients for popular providers that is light weight, fully-typed, and runtime-agnostic. It's built using oslo. Arctic offers OAuth 2.0 client library support for 50+ providers.\n\n## Oslo\n\nOslo provides simple, runtime agnostic, and fully-typed packages with minimal dependency for auth and cryptography. It includes a collection of auth utilities.\n\n## Auth.js\n\nAuth.js, formerly known as NextAuth.js, is now being maintained and overseen by the Better Auth team. It has long been one of the most widely used open source authentication libraries in the JavaScript ecosystem, and powers authentication for platforms like ChatGPT, Google Labs, and Cal.com.\n\n## Better Auth\n\nBetter Auth supports popular frameworks including React, Vue, Svelte, Astro, Solid, Next.js, Nuxt, Tanstack Start, Hono, and more. It provides multi-provider sign-in support including GitHub, Google, Discord, and Twitter.\n\n## Lucia\n\nLucia v3 will be deprecated by March 2025, and Lucia is now a learning resource on implementing auth from scratch.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."
