            "content": "Web search results for query: \"\"better-auth\" JWT authentication features Node.js 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"How to Use JWT and Node.js for Better App Security | Toptal®\",\"url\":\"https://www.toptal.com/json/jwt-nodejs-security\"},{\"title\":\"How To Use JSON Web Tokens (JWTs) in Express.js | DigitalOcean\",\"url\":\"https://www.digitalocean.com/community/tutorials/nodejs-jwt-expressjs\"},{\"title\":\"Node.js API Authentication\",\"url\":\"https://www.w3schools.com/nodejs/nodejs_api_auth.asp\"},{\"title\":\"JWT Authentication in Node.js: A Practical Guide | by Dev Balaji | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://dvmhn07.medium.com/jwt-authentication-in-node-js-a-practical-guide-c8ab1b432a49\"},{\"title\":\"Node.js Express JWT Authentication with MySQL & Roles\",\"url\":\"https://www.corbado.com/blog/nodejs-express-mysql-jwt-authentication-roles\"},{\"title\":\"Understanding JWT Authentication With Node.js [Updated]\",\"url\":\"https://www.simplilearn.com/tutorials/nodejs-tutorial/jwt-authentication\"},{\"title\":\"JWT Authentication In Node.js - GeeksforGeeks\",\"url\":\"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/node-js/jwt-authentication-with-node-js/\"},{\"title\":\"Node.js server-side authentication: Tokens vs. JWT - LogRocket Blog\",\"url\":\"https://blog.logrocket.com/node-js-server-side-authentication-tokens-vs-jwt/\"},{\"title\":\"OAuth or JWT? Everything Developers Need to Know in 2025 | by Nile Bits | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@nile.bits/oauth-or-jwt-everything-developers-need-to-know-in-2025-9212a031aff2\"},{\"title\":\"Authentication and JWT in Node.js - DEV Community\",\"url\":\"https://dev.to/eidorianavi/authentication-and-jwt-in-node-js-4i13\"}]\n\nI notice the search results don't specifically mention \"better-auth\" as a library or framework. Let me search more specifically for that project.\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - better-auth/better-auth: The most comprehensive authentication framework for TypeScript\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/better-auth/better-auth\"},{\"title\":\"Better Auth\",\"url\":\"https://www.better-auth.com/\"},{\"title\":\"Introduction | Better Auth\",\"url\":\"https://www.better-auth.com/docs/introduction\"},{\"title\":\"Installation | Better Auth\",\"url\":\"https://www.better-auth.com/docs/installation\"},{\"title\":\"Is Better Auth the key to solving authentication headaches? - LogRocket Blog\",\"url\":\"https://blog.logrocket.com/better-auth-authentication/\"},{\"title\":\"Client | Better Auth\",\"url\":\"https://www.better-auth.com/docs/concepts/client\"},{\"title\":\"Better Auth · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/better-auth\"},{\"title\":\"Better Auth: The authentication framework for TypeScript | Y Combinator\",\"url\":\"https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/better-auth\"},{\"title\":\"Basic Usage | Better Auth\",\"url\":\"https://www.better-auth.com/docs/basic-usage\"},{\"title\":\"better-auth - npm\",\"url\":\"https://www.npmjs.com/package/better-auth\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I now have comprehensive information about Better Auth and its JWT/authentication features. Here's what I found:\n\n## Better Auth: JWT Authentication Features\n\nBetter Auth is a framework-agnostic, universal authentication and authorization framework for TypeScript. It provides a comprehensive set of features out of the box and includes a plugin ecosystem that simplifies adding advanced functionalities.\n\n### Key JWT Authentication Features\n\nBetter Auth supports 2FA, passkey, multi-tenancy, multi-session support, and enterprise features like SSO and creating your own IDP.\n\nBetter Auth comes with built-in support for email/password and social sign-on providers. The library also supports less common authentication flows such as passkeys, usernames, and magic link authentication.\n\n### Node.js and TypeScript Support\n\nBetter Auth was designed from day one to be framework-agnostic, works seamlessly across multiple JavaScript frameworks while maintaining excellent type safety, and offers broad compatibility while deeply integrating with TypeScript. Better Auth supports a wide range of frameworks, including Vue, Svelte, Astro, Solid, Nuxt, Remix, and even backend frameworks like Express and Fastify.\n\n### Additional Advantages\n\nA notable feature is its database adapters with automatic schema generation and migration support, which significantly reduce the boilerplate work usually associated with setting up authentication. Better Auth is the recommended auth library by Next.js, Nuxt, Astro, and other top JS frameworks.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks.\n\n<system-reminder>\nThe task tools haven't been used recently. If you're working on tasks that would benefit from tracking progress, consider using TaskCreate to add new tasks and TaskUpdate to update task status (set to in_progress when starting, completed when done). Also consider cleaning up the task list if it has become stale. Only use these if relevant to the current work. This is just a gentle reminder - ignore if not applicable. Make sure that you NEVER mention this reminder to the user\n\n</system-reminder>",
