              "prompt": "Do a thorough security review of ALL code files in the Duxt/Dart todo API project at /Users/flakerimi/TMP/todo/. Focus on the server-side code:\n\nFiles to review:\n- server/api/auth.dart\n- server/api/todos.dart\n- server/middleware/auth_middleware.dart\n- server/utils/password.dart\n- server/utils/session_manager.dart\n- server/main.dart\n- server/db.dart\n- lib/models/user.dart\n- lib/models/todo.dart\n- lib/models/session.dart\n- pubspec.yaml\n\nCheck for these categories of security issues:\n1. Authentication/Authorization flaws (session management, cookie handling, password storage)\n2. Input validation gaps (missing validation, type confusion, injection)\n3. Information leakage (error messages, timing attacks, stack traces)\n4. OWASP Top 10 issues (injection, broken auth, sensitive data exposure, XSS, etc.)\n5. Session management issues (fixation, expiry, cookie flags)\n6. Race conditions or concurrency issues\n7. Missing security headers or CORS misconfiguration\n8. Dependency security concerns\n\nFor each issue found, note:\n- File and line number\n- Severity (Critical/High/Medium/Low/Info)\n- Description of the vulnerability\n- Recommended fix\n\nBe thorough — check every file. This is a READ-ONLY task, do not modify any files.",
